Hi there, 

Maddie here from Originality.AI

In this email, we'll cover a couple of topics! 

* Recent updates to Originality.AI Core App with added functionality

* The analysis of popular online review platforms, including Capterra,
G2, and TrustRadius.

* 

****Recent updates to our Core App: ****

We've recently made a few updates to our Core App which we would like
to highlight. This includes some new functionality that will enhance the
controls you have over your account and your team management. 

* 

**Session Tracking:**

* You can now track user logins and locations for enhanced security.

* 

**Role Assignments:**

* 

**Editors:**

* Editors can run content scans.

* 

**Managers:**

* Managers have the ability to oversee all scans and manage team
members.

* 

**Admins:**

* Admins act as the account holders owner's right hand, handling billing
and more (excluding subscriptions).

* Subscription management remains exclusive to the account owner.

Image below shows the new User Role Assignments 

**2. Analysis on Top Review Platforms: Capterra, G2, TrustRadius**

A little while ago, we asked for your input on the studies you'd like
us to conduct.  Your feedback on our previous studies
around AI-generated online reviews inspired us to dig deeper into some
of the more prominent platforms...this showed some interesting
trends! 

We conducted a **study**
which
analyzed 245,000 reviews about many different companies and products at 

**Capterra, G2, and TrustRadius**. These are popular sites for reviews
about B2B software. Our AI detector examined the text of these reviews
to find how much content was likely created by humans vs generated by
AI.

Here are some of the Key Findings: 

* AI-generated reviews range from 10% to 30% since the introduction of
ChatGPT, varying by platform.

* The higher the review ratings - the higher likelihood that is was
AI-generated

* G2 and TrustRadius exhibit recent declines in the percentage of
AI-generated reviews, potentially indicating improved

**AI-detection efforts** on these platforms. 

The study highlights the growing concern over the authenticity of the
online review-  casting doubt on their usefulness if a substantial
portion of them are potentially AI-generated. The limitations of current
verification processes highlight the need for exploring other solutions,
such as AI detectors, to address the challenges associated with ensuring
genuine and reliable user-generated reviews on popular platforms such as
Capterra, G2, and TrustRadius.

Check out the full study below! 

See Full Study

If you find these studies interesting and you'd like to see more of
them, let us know what you would like us to research! 

We hope you have a great end to your week- as always, don't hesitate to
reach out if you have any questions or concerns. 

Sent to: patriogabrielpatdu@gmail.com

Unsubscribe 

Jon Gillham, 1 First Street Suite #220, Collingwood, Ontario L9Y 1A1, Canada
